;">During the age of scaling law (2020 - 2021), since GPT-3 cannot outperfo=
rm fine-tuning T5-11B, and T5-11B is already troublesome to fine-tune, the =
community=E2=80=99s focus is more on prompting smaller models or parameter-=
efficient adaptation. Prefix tuning is one notable example in the intersect=
ion between prompting and adaptation, which was later partially unified by =
He et. al. 2021. The logic of our bets is simple: <span style=3D"font-weigh=
t:600" data-token-index=3D"1" class=3D"notion-enable-hover">if fine-tuning =
is better, we should put more effort into parameter-efficient tuning; if pr=
ompting is better, we should put more effort into training large language m=
odels.</span> </div></div></div></div><div data-block-id=3D"7152d1b1-2107-4=
